publish: allow — synthetic RSA test keypair used by the cosmon-rpp-adapter test
fixtures to sign and verify test tokens. It authorises nothing: no service, no
account, no environment ever trusted the matching public key. Tracked on purpose
so the fixtures are fixed and reviewable rather than regenerated per run.

The waiver is a sidecar rather than an inline marker because PEM has no comment
syntax — see `scripts/publish.sh`, `credential_waived_by_sidecar`.

If this key is ever pointed at anything real, delete this file first: the gate
is then supposed to red.

